<!--
  KHANDAQ (re-audit 2026-08-21, R-05) — release lint is a gate again, and it gates on ONE thing.

  Release lint had been switched off wholesale (checkReleaseBuilds false, abortOnError false), so
  none of it ran on the signing path. Simply turning it back on is not an option: this is an
  inherited TRIfA codebase and a real run produces 2378 findings — 52 Fatal and 69 Error, almost all
  of them missing translations and layout hygiene. A gate that red on day one gets switched off again
  within a week.

  So severity does the filtering. `all` and `Security` here are lint CATEGORY selectors, not issue
  ids: lint resolves a category name wherever an id is expected. Everything is demoted to warning,
  the Security category is promoted to fatal, and `lintVitalRelease` — which by construction runs
  only fatal issues — becomes exactly a security gate and nothing else. No hand-maintained list of
  security check ids to rot, and no 2 MB baseline snapshot that nobody has actually reviewed.

  Measured on this tree: the entire codebase has exactly ONE Security-category finding, the one
  excused below. Everything the re-audit worried lint would catch — exported components, cleartext
  traffic, trust-all TLS, allowBackup — is already clean.
-->
<lint>
    <issue id="all" severity="warning" />
    <issue id="Security" severity="fatal" />

    <!--
      The one Security finding in the tree, and it is a decision rather than a defect.

      DbSecretKeyStorage derives a DEVICE-BOUND key from ANDROID_ID (PBKDF2) to encrypt the database
      key's recovery backup. That is deliberate and argued in the file: the Keystore key is
      invalidated on some OS upgrades and dropped outright by some OEMs on reboot, and without a
      backup that survives it the user is permanently locked out at the password screen. ANDROID_ID
      is not used as a secret or an identity here — it is the device-binding factor that makes a
      stolen prefs file useless on its own.

      Scoped to the one file on purpose: a blanket ignore would also cover the next, unreviewed use.
    -->
    <issue id="HardwareIds">
        <ignore path="src/main/java/com/zoffcc/applications/trifa/DbSecretKeyStorage.java" />
    </issue>
</lint>
